Subacuática"},{"n":"Servicios Generales de la Armada","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":37.598869,"lo":-0.982697,"d":209},{"n":"Catedral de Santa María","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":37.599134,"lo":-0.984531,"d":272,"wp":"en:Cartagena Cathedral","ds":"The Cathedral of Cartagena in Spain, or the Cathedral of Santa María la Vieja, was a cathedral of the Diocese of Cartagena, located on the hill of La Concepción in the old town of Cartagena. It has been in ruins since 1939, when it was destroyed when Cartagena was shelled in the Spanish Civil War by Nationalist forces.","wpu":"Cartagena Cathedral","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Catedral_Cartagena.JPG/960px-Catedral_Cartagena.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Monument to the Heroes of Cavite and Santiago de Cuba","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":37.598204,"lo":-0.985807,"d":281,"wp":"es:Héroes de Cavite","ds":"The Monument to the Heroes of Cavite and Santiago de Cuba (Spanish: Monumento a los Héroes de Cavite y Santiago de Cuba) is an instance of public art and war memorial in Cartagena, Spain. It commemorates the role of the naval squadrons commanded by Patricio Montojo and Pascual Cervera during the 1898 Spanish–American War.","wpu":"Monument to the Heroes of Cavite and Santiago de Cuba","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Monument_of_the_heroes_of_Santiago_de_Cuba_and_Cavite_-_Cartagena_in_Spain_2016_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Monument_of_the_heroes_of_Santiago_de_Cuba_and_Cavite_-_Cartagena_in_Spain_2016_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Museo del Teatro Romano","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":37.598904,"lo":-0.985351,"d":296,"w":"https://teatroromano.cartagena.es","ph":"+34 968 525 149","wp":"es:Museo del Teatro Romano de Cartagena"},{"n":"Teatro Romano de Cartagena","g":"sights","k":"archaeological_site","la":37.599625,"lo":-0.9842,"d":310,"w":"https