.990225,"d":952},{"n":"Covadonga Calero","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":37.597961,"lo":-0.972118,"d":964},{"n":"Farmacia José Juan González 12H","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":37.604152,"lo":-0.989295,"d":969,"h":"Mo-Sa 09:00-22:00","ph":"+34 968 50 21 36"},{"n":"Banco Sabadell","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":37.597798,"lo":-0.971863,"d":985},{"n":"Despeñaperros Castle","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.6026,"lo":-0.9785,"d":738,"ds":"Despeñaperros Castle, also known as San José Castle, is a castle built in the 11th century in the historic center of Cartagena, Murcia Region in Spain. It was declared a cultural site on 7 August 1997. The walls are composed of masonry and generally flat.","wpu":"Despeñaperros Castle","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Castillodespenaperros.JPG/960px-Castillodespenaperros.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Punic wall of Cartagena","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.604167,"lo":-0.978611,"d":885,"ds":"The Punic wall of Cartagena (Spanish: Muralla púnica de Cartagena) is an archaeological site from the 3rd century BC in which can be seen the first defensive wall of Cartagena, built by the Carthaginians.","wpu":"Punic wall of Cartagena","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Carthaginian_wall_of_Cartagena.jpg/960px-Carthaginian_wall_of_Cartagena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Municipal Archaeological Museum of Cartagena","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.6154,"lo":-0.994,"d":2263,"ds":"The Municipal Archaeological Museum of Cartagena is an institution dedicated to the conservation, study, and exhibition of archaeological artifacts related to the municipality of Cartagena in the Region of Murcia, Spain. It is part of the Regional Network of Museums of Murcia.","wpu":"Municipal Archaeological Museum of Cartagena","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3c/MuseoarqueologicoCartagena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Escombreras","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":37.559444,"lo":-0.969167,"d":4350,"ds":"Escombreras is an islet within a natural park at the mouth of the port of Cartagena, Spain in the Region of Murcia. A breakwater was built in 2011 for the expansion of the port has hooked around the north side of the island, but it does not connect to it. The steep islet covers 4 hectares (9.9 acres).","wpu":"Escombreras","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a8/Escombreras.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Cartagena (Spanish: [kaɾtaˈxena] ) is a city in the Region of Murcia in Spain. As of 2024, with a population of 219,235, it is the second most populated municipality in the Region of Murcia. The city lies in a natural harbour of the Mediterranean coastline of the southeast of the Iberian Peninsula.","wpu":"Cartagena, Spain","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/Cartagena_palacio_consistorial5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}